/**
 * @mainpage RockBLOCK 960x Library
 *
 * @section intro_sec Introduction
 *
 * This is the official C library for the RockBLOCK 9602, 9603 and 9604
 * satellite modems. It enables sending and receiving data via the Iridium
 * network using Short Burst Data (SBD), and supports Linux, macOS, Windows
 * and Arduino platforms.
 *
 * The main documentation for this project is available in the
 * <a href="https://github.com/rock7/RockBLOCK-960x/blob/master/README.md">README.md</a>
 * of this repository. More specific documentation for the C library can be found below.
 *
 * This library also builds a shared library that powers the
 * rockblock960x Python package.
 *
 * @section features_sec Features
 *
 * - Simple high-level API to configure and use the RockBLOCK 960x via serial
 * - Synchronous and asynchronous SBD sessions
 * - Portable C99 core with a pluggable serial port layer
 * - Arduino and PlatformIO compatible
 *
 * @section usage_sec Getting Started
 *
 * See the main API in <a href="rockblock960x_8h.html">rockblock960x.h</a>.
 *
 * @section license_sec License
 *
 * MIT License — maintained by <a href="https://www.groundcontrol.com/">Ground Control</a>.
 */
